Um, you really don't need to start scum for 5+ mana if you want to do
the racket at 1 XL.  You can easily save 4 of your starting potions so
that you can fully heal your pet 4 times, and you can use your wand of
sleep if anything might do too much damage to your pet.

I also don't understand why they would die of starvation fairly
often.  It isn't that hard to get to some of the corpses before your
pet does, and due to healers automatically getting poison resistance,
they can eat the poisonous corpses that their pets will refuse to
eat.  Their pets will also refuse to eat lichen corpses, which can be
eaten by the healer.  This combined with #praying for food should
allow the healer to finish the protection racket without starving.

Also remember that most of the Minetown levels will have a food shop,
and even if they didn't have a food shop, if you were really paranoid
about food you could do a couple sokoban levels to stock up on food.

